#
#  ECMWF open data (IFS oper 0.25 degree, and AIFS single 0.25 degree) GRIB2 for
#  the Rust met_intermediate writer.  GRIB2 only: the GRIB1 parameter column is
#  blank on every row, so no GRIB1 message can match this table.
#
#  * Pressure levels carry both RH and SPECHUMD where the product publishes them;
#    AIFS publishes no pressure-level RH, so its init uses --use-spechumd yes.
#    HGT is derived from GEOPT / 9.81 on any level that carries no HGT (AIFS
#    publishes geopotential only).
#  * Soil is addressed by ordinal on the generalized vertical coordinate
#    (fixed-surface type 151): Level1/Level2 are the ordinal pair, not depths.
#    IFS publishes four layers, AIFS two (--nfgsoillevels 2).
#  * 2 m RH is derived from 2 m dewpoint (rrpr.F compute_rh_dewpt); SOILHGT from
#    surface geopotential; SNOW from snow depth in metres of water equivalent
#    (x 1000); SNOWH from SNOW and the published snow density.
#  * LANDSEA is the land fraction; the "ecmwf" map source converts it to a flag.
#  * Sea ice is not mapped: the product publishes ice thickness (10-2-1), not
#    the ice-cover fraction an init reads.
#  * Only instantaneous messages (product templates 4.0/4.1) match: the
#    statistically processed 2 m maximum and minimum temperatures share the
#    2 m temperature's identity and are dropped by met_intermediate.
